y  may need it the most and then on to a  sustainable growth path for the future  we also see a lot of startups using  credits to test new features or try out  products such as looker or firebase  details and conditions can be found at  cloud.google.com  they can also receive business support  you'll get tailored support from our  startup success team and our sales teams  with a single point of contact to help  you navigate google  attend special events meet google  engineers and specialists and even  connect with startup peers solving  similar challenges in the google cloud  startup community  they may even be co-marketing  opportunities with startups that you can  be invited to to co-create a case study  or be featured in a blog post now that  we've gone over what the google for  startups cloud program is let's talk  about how to qualify for it all  customers must be funded with publicly  verifiable equity investments up to and  including pre-seed angel seed and series  n  if series a this must have been raised  within the past 12 months  they must also have been founded within  10 years of applying to the program and  have a publicly available company  website and a unique company email  domain  if you need to create a custom email  account sign up for google workspace  you must also have a valid google cloud  billing account id linked to the domain  and company email on your application  additionally a customer must not be  already enrolled in the google for  startups cloud program or have received  an excess of four thousand dollars usd  in google cloud credits  you must also not be a company who is  ipo'd or been acquired or an educational  institution government entity nonprofit  personal blog dev shop consultancy or  agency  you must also not be a crypto mining  company or a company distributing tokens  contrary to regulatory guidance in your  jurisdiction  for example companies issuing tokens  solely for speculative purposes will not  be considered  apply a